    {
      "Seq": 11,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 26965,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I find myself in the village square, afternoon's warm light casting shadows. A well, a goose, a mounting block, stocks and a wayside cross loom as they once did in my childhood at the stable. I was drawn to the ways leading on from the stable. A church walk, a cattle pen, and a threshing floor all felt familiar, like a childhood memory of pushing through a storm. I let my focus go, where the stable animals once tormented me, and the storm pushed through with no legs.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 0,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 12,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 26965,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I spy a white goose, his neck stretched wide in a hiss. The smell alone is worth the strain to keep walking, for a laugh in the day is better than weeping.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 1,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 13,
      "Kind": 3,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 26965,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "Learned musk reading",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 0,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": null,
      "Key": "mm:Protagonist:musk_reading",
      "Lesson": true
    },
    {
      "Seq": 14,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 26965,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I have breathed in the scent of the goose, a musk that lingered in my breath. This success teaches me to be patient, for even the musk fades, leaving only the steady oak of my spirit.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 19,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 0,
      "Place": "Coast",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 26965,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I catch the scent of alertness from the goose, a white head stretched wide as a warning. He stinks of fear, his neck twitching with the threat of flight. I turn to the mounting block, scenting the earth's dampness and the tension in the air, posture of the stone steps warning of a horse's ready charge. I let my focus go, scenting the coast for signs of threat, my mind drifting as the breeze caressed my senses, warning in the very air.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 2,
      "Block": 0,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
