    {
      "Seq": 24,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Village",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 6800,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I hear the market murmur, sit at ease, and learn much from the gathered tales. Thank you for choosing our humble stall.",
      "Written": "",
      "State": 1,
      "Group": 3,
      "Block": 3,
      "Key": ""
    },
    {
      "Seq": 29,
      "Kind": 0,
      "Day": 5,
      "Place": "Village",
      "Area": "Square",
      "LocationId": 6800,
      "Actor": "Ghiulhiano Windhill",
      "ByCompanion": false,
      "Source": "I scent movement and hear a flick of an ear. These three stone steps warn of a horse's approach, a creature familiar from my own stallion's rhythmic breath. I catch the scent of alertness from the white goose, his neck stretched wide. It warns with every flick of his head, a kinship to beasts old and wild. I shift my scent, leading on. Here, a church walk, a cattle pen, and a threshing floor lead on, each with its own warning in the air and posture of the beasts.",
